{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549746-life-healing-vs-entropy-healing","id":1549746,"title":"Life Healing vs Entropy Healing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-04-02T12:22:07-07:00","id":1549746,"title":"Life Healing vs Entropy Healing","content":"So this question is pretty straightforward:<br /> <br /> Can Entropy 4 heal Lethal and Bashing damage the way Life 3 does? The book specifies it healing Aggravated, but mentions nothing about Lethal and Bashing. Personally, I'd say it does, but I'd like to hear your thoughts on this.<br /> <br /> And I have one more question: <br /> <br /> Does Entropy 4 require Quintessence to heal Aggravated the way Life 3 does? Additionally, does it follow the '2 successes for each level of Aggravated damage healed' rule?<br /> <br /> Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-02T13:56:50-07:00","id":1549750,"title":"","content":"Yes to all. If you can heal aggravated you definitely can heal lethal and bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T01:58:18-07:00","id":1549767,"title":"","content":"Thank you!<br /> <br /> So in this situation, what might prompt me to use Entropy 4 instead of Life 3? The lack of need to use auxiliar Spheres to heal other forms of Patterns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T04:34:31-07:00","id":1549770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Skeeper0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1549746-life-healing-vs-entropy-healing?p=1549767#post1549767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you!<br /> <br /> So in this situation, what might prompt me to use Entropy 4 instead of Life 3? The lack of need to use auxiliar Spheres to heal other forms of Patterns?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Entropy alone can be uaed to affect other splats (vampire, garou), if that's what you mean. I'd say that to affect their pattern directly you still need the spheres combinations, but then that would make Entropy pointless in the spell.<br /> <br /> Well, you can definitely damage them with Entropy alone by affecting their surroundings, but healing require direct pattern manipulation. <br /> <br /> And why use Entropy 4 instead of Life 3? Because you may not have Life 3. If you do, use it at a lower difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T07:53:47-07:00","id":1549775,"title":"","content":"Entropy 4 attacks are also direct pattern manipulation, which is why they are Agg by default. <br /> <br /> I do think Entropy 4 can attack vampires, though this is not a special property. Mages have to add Matter to Life for magical attacks on Vampires, and by Entropy 4, Entropy can target both living and material patterns. Entropy gets to affect thoughts and minds at rank 5, so at that rank a mage could probably make an attack on the Fae without Mind. Whether Entropy 4 can make full attacks on the Fera without help depends on if we consider Spirit to fall under the living patterns of rank 4, the thought patterns of rank 5, or no rank of Entropy. <br /> <br /> Honestly, I can see arguments for Entropy 4 being able to attack almost anything without help, but I don't know for sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-03T16:10:29-07:00","id":1549783,"title":"","content":"Thank you guys, you have been very insightful!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13197-skeeper0","name":"Skeeper0","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-04-04T17:52:27-07:00","id":1549834,"title":"","content":"I personally make the biggest difference being description of the result. Entropic healing isn't so much &quot;healing&quot;, but making the systemic state of the body to not collapse. That means any damage is still visually there, just not worsening or hindering the target anymore. How much of a problem that is, is another story.<br /> <br /> When I <b>really</b> see the need to limit Entropy healing in some way, I make it a continuous effect: if the effect ends before <i>actual</i> healing, the damage comes back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}